      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el75",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 302003102,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 893149981,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1720,
      "y": 223,
      "width": 546.0,
      "height": 390.0,
      "text": "INDEX       Client -> Gateway -> Ingest -> Postgres\n                                          ( + S3 when > 256 KB )\n\nSEARCH      Client -> Gateway -> Search -> Redis -> Elasticsearch\n\nFETCH       Client -> Gateway -> Doc    -> Redis -> Postgres (primary)\n\nDOWNLOAD    Client -> Gateway -> Doc    -> Postgres -> 302\n            then the CLIENT fetches the bytes from S3 directly\n\nDELETE      Client -> Gateway -> Doc    -> Postgres\n            soft:  status = DELETED, nothing removed yet\n\nASYNC       Postgres -> Debezium -> Kafka -> Indexer\n            Indexer  ->  S3        read /raw, write /text\n                     ->  Elastic   index, or delete by doc_id\n                     ->  Redis     INCR inv, DEL the doc key\n                     ->  Postgres  status = LIVE\n\nFAILURE     Kafka -> retry.30s -> retry.5m -> retry.30m -> DLQ\n            transient only.  permanent errors go straight to FAILED.\n\nRETENTION   Retention Job -> S3\n            purge /raw and /text after the 30 day undelete window",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "INDEX       Client -> Gateway -> Ingest -> Postgres\n                                          ( + S3 when > 256 KB )\n\nSEARCH      Client -> Gateway -> Search -> Redis -> Elasticsearch\n\nFETCH       Client -> Gateway -> Doc    -> Redis -> Postgres (primary)\n\nDOWNLOAD    Client -> Gateway -> Doc    -> Postgres -> 302\n            then the CLIENT fetches the bytes from S3 directly\n\nDELETE      Client -> Gateway -> Doc    -> Postgres\n            soft:  status = DELETED, nothing removed yet\n\nASYNC       Postgres -> Debezium -> Kafka -> Indexer\n            Indexer  ->  S3        read /raw, write /text\n                     ->  Elastic   index, or delete by doc_id\n                     ->  Redis     INCR inv, DEL the doc key\n                     ->  Postgres  status = LIVE\n\nFAILURE     Kafka -> retry.30s -> retry.5m -> retry.30m -> DLQ\n            transient only.  permanent errors go straight to FAILED.\n\nRETENTION   Retention Job -> S3\n            purge /raw and /text after the 30 day undelete window",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
