    },
    {
      "id": "el78",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1564070057,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2036465043,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1720,
      "y": 744.0,
      "width": 514.8,
      "height": 455.0,
      "text": "SERVICES        rectangles\n\n  API Gateway     verify JWT, inject tenant / user / session,\n                  STRIP any inbound X-Tenant-Id\n  Search          GET /search  \u00b7  L1 in-process LRU, 5 s\n  Doc             GET /documents/{id}, /raw, /text  \u00b7  DELETE\n  Ingest          POST /documents  \u00b7  :negotiate  \u00b7  :commit\n  Debezium        reads the Postgres WAL, replaces an outbox table\n  Indexer         extract, index, invalidate.  one consumer per\n                  partition, so 32 is the ceiling\n  Retention Job   nightly purge of soft-deleted bytes\n\n\nDATASTORES      circles\n\n  Postgres        source of truth.  primary + 2 read replicas.\n                  metadata always, body when <= 256 KB\n  S3              /raw immutable, /text derived and rebuildable\n  Elasticsearch   24 shards x 1 replica, routing = tenant_id\n  Redis           rate-limit counters, query cache, doc cache\n  Kafka           doc.index.v1, 32 partitions, key = doc_id\n\n\nTHE THREE ISOLATION LAYERS\n\n  gateway   X-Tenant-Id minted from the JWT, inbound stripped\n  query     term filter on tenant_id, injected by the repo layer\n  cache     every Redis key is tenant-prefixed",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SERVICES        rectangles\n\n  API Gateway     verify JWT, inject tenant / user / session,\n                  STRIP any inbound X-Tenant-Id\n  Search          GET /search  \u00b7  L1 in-process LRU, 5 s\n  Doc             GET /documents/{id}, /raw, /text  \u00b7  DELETE\n  Ingest          POST /documents  \u00b7  :negotiate  \u00b7  :commit\n  Debezium        reads the Postgres WAL, replaces an outbox table\n  Indexer         extract, index, invalidate.  one consumer per\n                  partition, so 32 is the ceiling\n  Retention Job   nightly purge of soft-deleted bytes\n\n\nDATASTORES      circles\n\n  Postgres        source of truth.  primary + 2 read replicas.\n                  metadata always, body when <= 256 KB\n  S3              /raw immutable, /text derived and rebuildable\n  Elasticsearch   24 shards x 1 replica, routing = tenant_id\n  Redis           rate-limit counters, query cache, doc cache\n  Kafka           doc.index.v1, 32 partitions, key = doc_id\n\n\nTHE THREE ISOLATION LAYERS\n\n  gateway   X-Tenant-Id minted from the JWT, inbound stripped\n  query     term filter on tenant_id, injected by the repo layer\n  cache     every Redis key is tenant-prefixed",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
